A note on precision: I was able to verify the **onchain** flow (the `GenerateReport → writeReport → Forwarder → onReport` sequence, the report contents, and the accountability rationale) directly against Chainlink's docs. The **offchain** description reflects the general CRE model of returning trigger responses rather than writing onchain; the exact return-shape depends on your trigger type (HTTP, cron, log, etc.), so check the specific trigger guide for your use case. Want me to tailor either path to a concrete trigger (e.g., an HTTP-triggered price workflow) with full runnable code?
